boutthefed/ed…", "end": 204, "expanded_url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/aboutthefed/educational-tools/national-high-school-fed-challenge.htm", "images": [{"height": 800, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2117287469804867584/5RADje8D?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 800}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2117287469804867584/5RADje8D?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 181, "status": 200, "title": "National High School Fed Challenge", "unwound_url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/aboutthefed/educational-tools/national-high-school-fed-challenge.htm", "url": "https://t.co/l2eFF6tYKr"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/mjnX6FsuqT", "end": 228, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/federalreserve/status/2117287423868899544/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2117287380856053760", "start": 205, "url": "https://t.co/mjnX6FsuqT"}]}, "id": "2117287423868899544", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 29611, "like_count": 35, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 12, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "High school students from across the nation can compete in the 2026-2027 national High School Fed Challenge. Register by February 15, 2027.\n#EconTwitter\n#HSFedChallenge\nLearn more: https://t.co/l2eFF6tYKr https://t.co/mjnX6FsuqT", "url": "https://x.com/federalreserve/status/2117287423868899544"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-11-02T15:35:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117279363175739630"], "id": "2117279363175739630", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 121, "impression_count": 40884, "like_count": 838, "quote_count": 17, "reply_count": 231, "retweet_count": 44}, "text": "When you think about the Labs' weird approach to software (sudden changes, bad communication), it is worth remembering that a core belief is that these products are a temporary thing they have to do to raise money for a couple years until \"true\" AGI makes all products obsolete.", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2117279363175739630"}, {"author_id": "15072071", "created_at": "2026-11-02T15:31:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117278327429791882"], "id": "2117278327429791882", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 2350, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "In today's post, the authors discuss insights from their recent research on the role of banking supervision in identifying &amp; disciplining failing banks &amp; show that bank failures typically result from supervisory closure decisions based on hard information about book equity.", "url": "https://x.com/NewYorkFed/status/2117278327429791882"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-11-02T15:16:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117274560018182375"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/econvitals/sta…", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/econvitals/status/2117210211903529188", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/LmdvjVoQr5"}]}, "id": "2117274560018182375", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 87, "impression_count": 21279, "like_count": 158, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 17, "retweet_count": 15}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117210211903529188", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "My favorite new proprietary measure is \"Econvitals Underlying Unit Labor Costs\".\n\nIt blends five wage measures (weighted by inverse variance), re-means to match PCE and adjusts for how productivity growth different in this cycle than the past.\n\nConsistent with ~2% inflation now. https://t.co/LmdvjVoQr5", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2117274560018182375"}, {"author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-11-02T15:01:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117270806581670112"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Artificial intelligence (AI) has the potential to raise productivity, strengthen medium‑term growth, and support economic diversification across the Middle East, North Africa, Afghanistan, and Pakistan (MENAP) and the Caucasus and Central Asia (CCA). However, prospective gains are uneven, reflecting substantial cross‑country differences in AI exposure, preparedness, and access to advanced technologies. Without targeted policy action, AI risks widening existing development and income gaps. This paper argues that AI‑related policy priorities should be closely aligned with countries’ levels of preparedness. Economies with strong digital infrastructure, skills, and institutional capacity should focus on strengthening digital innovation ecosystems and adapting legal and regulatory frameworks to support and govern rapid AI diffusion. Countries with more limited preparedness should prioritize expanding basic digital infrastructure and investing in human capital to capture early productivity g", "display_url": "imf.org/en/publication…", "end": 211, "expanded_url": "https://www.imf.org/en/publications/departmental-papers-policy-papers/issues/2026/09/29/harnessing-artificial-intelligences-potential-in-the-middle-east-and-central-asia-574898", "images": [{"height": 405, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2117246491081547776/zvFQEtML?format=png&name=orig", "width": 400}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2117246491081547776/zvFQEtML?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 188, "status": 200, "title": "Harnessing Artificial Intelligence’s Potential in the Middle East and Central Asia", "unwound_url": "https://www.imf.org/en/publications/departmental-papers-policy-papers/issues/2026/09/29/harnessing-artificial-intelligences-potential-in-the-middle-east-and-central-asia-574898", "url": "https://t.co/EZ5Il00ght"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/OvWIoXI1wx", "end": 235, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2117270806581670112/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2117270516516171776", "start": 212, "url": "https://t.co/OvWIoXI1wx"}]}, "id": "2117270806581670112", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 17691, "like_count": 55, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 11, "retweet_count": 18}, "text": "The Caucasus and Central Asia is already on par with emerging-market peers on AI preparedness — and there's scope to go further. Innovation and regulation are where the biggest gains lie. https://t.co/EZ5Il00ght https://t.co/OvWIoXI1wx", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2117270806581670112"}, {"author_id": "1831398480700428289", "created_at": "2026-11-02T14:00:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117255589667455421"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/KZU2RWNufC", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Yoshua_Bengio/status/2117255589667455421/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2117253437012267008", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/KZU2RWNufC"}]}, "id": "2117255589667455421", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 18, "impression_count": 6989, "like_count": 178, "quote_count": 8, "reply_count": 18, "retweet_count": 46}, "text": "I was pleased to give remarks at the start of the Digital Summit in Berlin this afternoon. Frontier AI companies continue to push model capabilities further and faster forward, without a convincing plan to make the technology safer. This dynamic carries significant risks to https://t.co/KZU2RWNufC", "url": "https://x.com/Yoshua_Bengio/status/2117255589667455421"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "39125788", "name": "Ethan Mollick", "username": "emollick"}, {"id": "612896910", "name": "BLS-Labor Statistics", "username": "BLS_gov"}, {"id": "25098482", "name": "IMF", "username": "IMFNews"}, {"id": "332617373", "name": "Mohamed A. El-Erian", "username": "elerianm"}, {"id": "279036722", "name": "Jason Furman", "username": "jasonfurman"}, {"id": "1161370756208648193", "name": "FedResearch", "username": "FedResearch"}, {"id": "26538229", "name": "Federal Reserve", "username": "federalreserve"}, {"id": "68746721", "name": "François Chollet", "username": "fchollet"}, {"id": "321536046", "name": "BEA News", "username": "BEA_News"}, {"id": "15072071", "name": "New York Fed", "username": "NewYorkFed"}, {"id": "18313984807004